{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_research_2026_09_02_second_probe_consumer_and_snapshot_research_note", "label": "Research note: the second probe (2026-09-02)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/research/2026-09-02-second-probe-consumer-and-snapshot.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "What the platform did, as opposed to what the documentation says: consumer versioning, cubic sequencing, memory snapshot cost, retry timing, storage TTL."}, {"id": "docs_research_2026_09_02_second_probe_consumer_and_snapshot_wasm_probe_2", "label": "wasm-probe-2 throwaway app", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/research/2026-09-02-second-probe-consumer-and-snapshot.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Node v24.18.0 arm64, memoryMB 1024, Pyodide 314.0.6 with the tools, service/app.py, two datasets, fifty asks and a 30 MB snapshot in a 17.0 MB assets.js; every SHA-256 matched native Python 3.14.7. Installation f52bde9e on the dev site, version 3.2.0."}, {"id": "docs_research_2026_09_02_second_probe_consumer_and_snapshot_consumer_is_minor_version", "label": "Adding a consumer is a minor version; a remote is major", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/research/2026-09-02-second-probe-consumer-and-snapshot.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "2.0.0 to 2.1.0 on adding consumer, function and timeoutSeconds 300; raising to 900 also minor. Adding a remote stopped for --approve MAJOR_VERSION_RULE (data residency or egress modification); removing it was minor. Settled by deploy, the rule CLAUDE.md sets."}, {"id": "docs_research_2026_09_02_second_probe_consumer_and_snapshot_sequencing_is_cubic", "label": "Sequencing is cubic in the ask count", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/research/2026-09-02-second-probe-consumer-and-snapshot.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Native 2 asks 0.17 s, 4 1.1 s, 8 7.0 s, 12 21 s, 16 48 s; fifty did not finish in ten minutes. Forge plain runtime ten times slower: 12 asks 209 s, 16 asks 479 s; twenty would not fit 900 s. Every earlier per-ask pricing, including ADR 0031's, is wrong by this shape."}, {"id": "docs_research_2026_09_02_second_probe_consumer_and_snapshot_memory_snapshot", "label": "Pyodide memory snapshot trade-off", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/research/2026-09-02-second-probe-consumer-and-snapshot.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "makeMemorySnapshot cuts cold start from 11 s to 1.3 s but costs 1.65x on every computation afterwards, measured A/B in one container; Forge's runtime, not Pyodide's. Suits the synchronous resolver function, not the consumer."}, {"id": "docs_research_2026_09_02_second_probe_consumer_and_snapshot_consumer_retry_in_forty_seconds", "label": "A timed-out consumer retries in about 40 seconds", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/research/2026-09-02-second-probe-consumer-and-snapshot.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Not the fifteen-minute ceiling documented; retryContext arrives; getJob().cancel() stopped it; getStats() reported zeros mid-retry and is no use as a status source. The retry guard is more urgent than ADR 0031 said."}, {"id": "docs_research_2026_09_02_second_probe_consumer_and_snapshot_forecast_barely_grows_with_board_size", "label": "Forecast barely grows with board size", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/research/2026-09-02-second-probe-consumer-and-snapshot.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "route_forecast 1.52 s 